<h2>Questions from Rochester property owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Does appraisal help with a flood claim in Rochester?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Appraisal only applies to covered losses. If your damage comes from surface flooding, it is generally covered by flood insurance rather than a homeowner policy, and that policy has its own dispute process. Sewer backup under an endorsement can often go to appraisal.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you inspect outside Rochester city limits?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. We serve owners across Olmsted County and the rest of southeastern Minnesota.</p></div></details></div>
